                                                "sense_id": "d977dec9-87ac-37af-8ed9-953cf0af2708",
                                                "text": "It [the dáo of the Nágá tribe, south-east of Assam] is a thick, heavy backsword, eighteen inches long, with a bevel where the point should be, worn at the waist in a half-scabbard of wood, and used for digging as well as killing."
